  "changes_after_first_run": "The test fixed before the first run -- fit 1981 to 2010, test 2011 onward -- failed, and in the direction that costs the buyer rather than the pool: 80 of 870 seasons fell below the fitted 1 in 5 year low where 174 were expected. The same gamma describes the seasons it was fitted on (359 of 1740 against 348), so the distribution is not what failed. What changed is the rain: across these stations a season since 2011 has averaged about a tenth above its own long run mean, against about a tenth below in the 1980s. The published normals are therefore fitted on the most recent 30 seasons and not on the whole record, the same change the extremes build made for the same reason. A price from the old window would have been roughly twice what the measured seasons support."
